% ============================================================================
% newton-laws.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics newton-laws library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is Newton's second
% law called?": it states no physics fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `newton_law` rows and returns the short name + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the name
% action_reaction, recall the law number that has it — 3). There is no fourth
% law of motion, so a recall on number 4 abstains honestly — the engine never
% invents a law.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli newton-laws.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "newton-laws.adj"

? newton_law(1, $Name)                % expect inertia
? newton_law(2, $Name)                % expect force
? newton_law(3, $Name)                % expect action_reaction
? newton_law($N, action_reaction)     % expect 3 — reverse recall
? newton_law(4, $Name)                % expect abstain — there is no fourth law of motion
